Deckrunner is an unofficial fan project, unaffiliated with Electronic Arts or CD PROJEKT RED. It contains no Skate 3 or
Cyberpunk 2077 code or data; players build what it needs from their own copies with its setup.

This product builds on the following third-party work.

SK8V (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/becaring/SK8V, Copyright 2026 becaring.
  Deckrunner's runtime (red4ext\plugins\deckrunner\runtime\deckrunner_runtime.dll) is built on SK8V's Skate runtime
  and its crates, including skate-aems (Skate 3's audio runtime) and skate-hud. The setup runs SK8V 1.1.10's
  preparation scripts unchanged (setup\sk8v\tools: xiso.py, _common.py, convert-skate-data.py, prepare-skate-audio.py,
  prepare-audio-tuning.py; setup\sk8v\LICENSE and setup\sk8v\NOTICE are SK8V's own), and setup\get-python.ps1 is
  SK8V's. Their two programs, skate-xma.exe and xex_image.exe, built unchanged from SK8V 1.1.10, are not in this
  download (Nexus Mods does not allow programs in mod files): the setup fetches them from Deckrunner's GitHub release,
  https://github.com/londonbrown/Deckrunner/releases/tag/setup-tools-1 (pinned SHA-256).

Skate engine (Apache-2.0)
  2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup, by chasmlol, a fork of IW4L by vladtrc. https://github.com/chasmlol/2010-rust-rewrite-mashup
  Its Skate 3 engine crates (skate-core, skate-data, skate-host, skate-net) are compiled into the runtime, with SK8V's
  modifications.

Skate 3 HUD and asset pipeline (Apache-2.0 by grant)
  skate-3-rust-engine, by chasmlol, used under chasmlol's Apache-2.0 grant of 2026-10-07 at commit cb796893 (see SK8V's
  NOTICE). https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine
  The setup runs its asset-pipeline exports from the snapshot in setup\sk8v\upstream\skate-3-rust-engine-donor.

EA-XMA audio decoder (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  skate-xma.exe, in Deckrunner's setup-tools release (not in this download), is SK8V's port of FFmpeg 4.4's
  xmaframes / WMA Pro decoder (libavcodec), Copyright the FFmpeg developers, https://ffmpeg.org: a separate program
  under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later, with its complete source inside that release's zip.

RED4ext.SDK (MIT)
  https://github.com/WopsS/RED4ext.SDK, Copyright (c) 2020 - present Octavian Dima (WopsS). Linked into the plugin.

WolvenKit (GPL-3.0), not included
  https://github.com/WolvenKit/WolvenKit. The setup downloads WolvenKit's official command-line release (pinned version
  and SHA-256) onto the player's PC. setup\wkprobe\wkprobe.dll links it and is therefore licensed under the GNU General
  Public License 3.0 or later (setup\wkprobe\LICENSE); its complete source is in setup\wkprobe\source.

.NET runtime (MIT), not included
  wkprobe runs on .NET 10. If none is installed, the setup downloads Microsoft's official .NET 10 runtime zip
  (pinned SHA-512) into its work folder.

Python, numpy and Pillow, not included
  If the player has no suitable Python, setup\get-python.ps1 (SK8V's) downloads the official embeddable Python and the numpy
  and Pillow wheels (each checked against its published SHA-256). Each keeps its own licence.

Rust crates
  Every other crate linked into the runtime keeps its own licence: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt lists them with their
  licence texts.

